{"author":{"id":"29588b87a98184856c6eb9104921c34cca98a9cb029a2ee86cc10622d693ba86"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794791543,"nonce":"CToSRfYAIxx4Pj/PAfTwsu+nUOk=","title":"Div::on_click bubbles to every ancestor and cannot be stopped","message":"A click on a child with an on_click handler also runs the on_click handlers of all its ancestors. EventContext has no stop_propagation (only an internal propagation_stopped field in interactive.rs).\n\nReproducer (blinc_layout 0.6.0, offscreen with EventRouter): a card div with on_click select, containing a button div with on_click move. Click the button: the button handler runs, then the card handler runs. In a kanban board the click on the grab button also ran the drop handler of the card and column, so the card was put down at once.\n\nExpected: a handler can stop the event from reaching ancestors, or a div can be marked as not receiving bubbled clicks.\n\nWorkaround in the caller: handlers on siblings instead of ancestors, plus a shared flag that the ancestor checks.\n\nStand: waits for the Blinc team / fork; no change made here.","files":null}]}